Bundled third-party software
============================

drogonR is licensed under MIT. Vendored dependencies use their own
licenses: Drogon — MIT, Trantor — 3-clause BSD, JsonCpp — MIT/Public
Domain, wepoll — 2-clause BSD. All are compatible with the MIT license
of drogonR itself.

This package bundles the following third-party libraries in `src/drogon/`,
which are compiled together with the package source.

1. Drogon (https://github.com/drogonframework/drogon)
   Copyright (c) 2019-2023 An Tao and contributors
   License: MIT
   Source: src/drogon/lib/

2. Trantor (https://github.com/an-tao/trantor)
   Copyright (c) 2016-2021 An Tao and contributors
   License: 3-clause BSD (compatible with MIT)
   Source: src/drogon/trantor/
   Note: Trantor is derived from the Muduo library
         Copyright (c) 2010, Shuo Chen, also under 3-clause BSD.

3. JsonCpp (https://github.com/open-source-parsers/jsoncpp)
   Original author: Baptiste Lepilleur
   Current maintainer: Christopher Dunn
   See src/drogon/third_party/jsoncpp/AUTHORS for the full contributor list.
   License: MIT (or Public Domain at the user's choice)
   Source: src/drogon/third_party/jsoncpp/

4. wepoll (https://github.com/piscisaureus/wepoll)
   Copyright (c) 2012-2020 Bert Belder
   License: 2-clause BSD
   Source: src/drogon/third_party/wepoll/
   Note: Compiled and linked only on Windows builds. Provides epoll(7)
         emulation on top of Windows IOCP, used by Trantor's poller
         under _WIN32.

The full text of each license is preserved alongside the corresponding
source tree. The bundled sources have been minimally modified for use
inside an R package; modifications are clearly marked in the affected
files (search for `DROGONR` in comments).
